      "Full current hashes and the complete partition/root reduction precede ownership transfer. After the existing material.take boundary, the new code adds only infallible normal-return selection/accounting; no new callback, authorization, fallible Result or externally observable partial publication is introduced.",
      "The existing tree-too-large successful fallback may clear optional retained material, unchanged from bebb. This review does not claim allocation-panic/OOM transactional recovery or a new unwind guarantee.",
      "Old string ownership moves on success; no old value allocation is released or credited while a fallible input is still being collected. The transient index is dropped with the builder."
    ],
    "equality_and_hashes": [
      "Private immutable PlainValue contains complete canonical bytes, including delimiters. Cheap ValueIndex(length, first/last bytes) is only a one-candidate lookup accelerator.",
      "Occupied candidates share an Arc only after equality of every current encoded byte. A same-index different-value collision independently allocates/charges the new value and neither replaces nor expands the candidate bucket.",
      "Each full key retains its own originally computed key/leaf hashes. Cold add_encoded computes original hashes before optional retention; key/value misses keep original encoding and hashing.",
      "Warm try_plain_json_string and add_encoded require exact full-key and complete-value equality. No allocation pointer or cheap index is a mathematical or authorization cache key.",
      "Original M06 complete grammar/count pass, wire limits, leaf collision check, complete State binding and full derive encode_for_cache remain outside this patch and byte-identical."
    ],
    "accounting": [
      "The final retained set charges key bytes and ExactString descriptors per entry, PlainValue descriptor and boxed bytes once per actual selected allocation, a conservative four-usize Arc/alignment allowance, plus the string-array handle and cached charge field.",
      "Arc::as_ptr is used solely for billing identity. A value enters paid_values only after its entry fits; selected entries keep those pointers alive until publication, preventing pointer reuse during accounting.",
      "Equal contents in distinct allocations are charged separately. A pending new key borrowing a prior Arc pays that value in the final set when no prior key survives.",
      "Tree arrays retain priority; the pending budget subtracts all still-live prior material and gives no premature replacement credit. The stored string_charge_bytes is set only for a completed immutable material.",
      "The original two-MiB payload and sixteen-MiB retained-software-charge ceilings remain unchanged. Temporary leaves/index/Arc references and allocator peak RSS are not certified by the retained-material limit."
